<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Q4 GDP unchanged, 1996 GDP fell 0.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Swiss Q4 GDP unchanged, 1996 GDP fell 0.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Gross Domestic Product (GDP) was unchanged on a annualised, seasonally-adjusted basis in the fourth quarter of 1996 compared to the third quarter, the Federal Office for Economic Policy said.</p>
<p>The third-quarter decline was revised to 0.6 percent from the 0.7 percent originally reported.</p>
<p>For all of 1996, GDP fell 0.7 percent compared with 1995. GDP had risen 0.1 percent in 1995.  </p>
<p>GDP at 1980 prices. Percentage changes versus previous quarter, seasonally adjusted, projected on annual basis:</p>
<p>					 Q4 1996     Q3 1996    Q4 1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	  0.0	  -0.6	 -0.3</p>
<p> Private household consumption+1.0	  -0.1	 -0.9</p>
<p> Public sector consumption    -0.2	  +0.6	 -0.6</p>
<p> Fixed asset investment	 -1.7	  -0.9	 +6.1</p>
<p> Domestic demand		  +1.2	  -0.9	 -0.4</p>
<p> Exports			    +0.9	  +1.0	 +3.7</p>
<p> Imports			    +3.1	  +0.3	 +3.0</p>
<p>Percentage changes compared with corresponding quarter of previous year.</p>
<p>					 Q4 1996     Q3 1996    Q4 1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	   -0.6	  -0.9	 -0.6</p>
<p> Private household consumption  +0.8	  -0.3	 -0.1</p>
<p> Public sector consumption	 0.0	  +0.2	 -0.2</p>
<p> Fixed asset investment	   +0.2	  +2.9	 +0.6</p>
<p> Domestic demand		    -1.2	  -0.1	 +0.9</p>
<p> Exports				+2.1	  +1.5	 +1.3</p>
<p> Imports				+0.8	  +2.9	 +4.3</p>
</text>
